diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index e6dab90..f09dbce 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -2,10 +2,30 @@ # Kraftrack
 
 Existing Kraftrack product: Laravel, Vue 3, Inertia, and Tailwind. Login, artisan dashboard, work logs, public profiles, and admin chrome are unchanged from the current app.
 
-Additive admin work sits at `/admin/staff` (operations roles) and `/admin/users` (artisan directory). Login, artisan dashboard, work logs, and existing chrome are unchanged.
+Additive admin work sits at:
+
+- `/admin/staff` — **Access & Roles** (what operations staff can *do* on the platform)
+- `/admin/users` — artisan directory
+- `/admin/hr` — **People / HR** (who staff *are* as employees: profile, leave, payroll, performance, documents)
+
+Login, artisan dashboard, work logs, and existing chrome are unchanged.
 
 On Users, **View** opens a right-hand detail panel. The slide uses a GPU `transform` only — no width/left animation — so it eases in cleanly.
 
+## People / HR module (`/admin/hr`)
+
+An internal-facing HR tool, separate from Access & Roles. Super Admin only.
+
+- **Directory & profile** — tabbed profile (Overview, Leave, Payroll, Performance, Documents). Staff can be marked **exited** without deleting their history; exiting prompts a reminder to revoke platform access in Access & Roles (the two systems are not synced).
+- **Leave** — configurable leave types with allowances, per-staff balances, an approval workflow (pending → approved/rejected/cancelled), a shared team calendar, and guards against overlapping requests and negative balances (an approver can override, and it is logged).
+- **Payroll** — per-staff compensation (base + custom allowances) and payslips with PDF export. Compensation edits require a logged reason. Gated behind dedicated `hr.payroll.*` permissions and hidden from anyone without them — enforced server-side, not just in the UI. It records what is owed/paid and does not move money (`// TODO: connect to payout provider …`).
+- **Performance** — a lightweight, dated note timeline with an optional rating.
+- **Documents** — per-profile storage with a type tag, optional expiry, and an expiry alert.
+- **Checklists** — editable onboarding / offboarding templates attached to a profile and checked off.
+- **Reports** — headcount, leave utilisation, payroll cost (gated), and performance coverage, each exportable to CSV.
+
+Staff currently on approved leave are flagged as **On leave** wherever they appear (including the Access & Roles staff list).
+
 ## Run locally
 
 ```bash
